      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Taking an additional 200mg of caffeine without consulting your doctor can be problematic. The recommended daily caffeine intake varies from person to person, but excessive consumption (more than 400mg per day) can lead to adverse effects like jitteriness, anxiety, and an irregular heartbeat. Additionally, combining caffeine with other stimulants, including prescription medications like Ritalin, can increase the risk of unwanted side effects. Would you like some tips on prioritizing your study sessions or self-motivation?",
      "source": "target",
